Story #69 is complete and committed. Exiting normally — more stories remain (`passes: false` for #70 onward), so the ralph loop will re-invoke for the next one.

## Summary — Story #69: scroll wheel changing number input values

**Fix:** Added `onWheel={(e) => e.currentTarget.blur()}` to all 7 `<input type="number">` elements in the renderer:
- `TimerSettingsContent.tsx` — cookie min/hr, default reps, break duration, long-break interval, long-break duration (5)
- `ProjectsSettingsContent.tsx` — auto-archive value (1)
- `TimerPlayButton.tsx` — start-dialog Reps (1)

Scrolling over a focused number input now scrolls the page and deselects the input instead of silently incrementing the value. `blur()` was chosen over `preventDefault()` so page scroll keeps working.

**Verification:**
- `grep -rn onWheel src/` → exactly 7 handlers, one per input ✓
- `npm run typecheck` → zero errors ✓
